.TH ROUND 3 "2026-05-10" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
round \- round to nearest integer, ties away from zero
.SH LIBRARY
Math Library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "double round(double " x ");"
.PP
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "float roundf(float " x ");"
.PP
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "long double roundl(long double " x ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR round ()
function rounds
.I x
to the nearest integral value.
When the fractional part is exactly 0.5, it rounds away from zero.
.PP
The
.BR roundf ()
and
.BR roundl ()
functions are float and long double variants, respectively.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR round ()
functions return the rounded integral value.
.br
If the result cannot be represented, the return value is unspecified.
.SH ERRORS
No errors are defined.
The functions do not set
.IR errno .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
printf("\\%f\\n", round(0.5));   /* prints 1.0 */
printf("\\%f\\n", round(1.5));   /* prints 2.0 */
printf("\\%f\\n", round(2.5));   /* prints 3.0 */
printf("\\%f\\n", round(-0.5));  /* prints -1.0 */
printf("\\%f\\n", round(-1.5));  /* prints -2.0 */
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ceil (3),
.BR floor (3),
.BR trunc (3),
.BR roundeven (3),
.BR rint (3)
